course: dictionary
lesson: 5404
title: Krill, the tiny giants of the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Krill are tiny sea animals that look a bit like shrimp. They swim in huge groups in cold oceans, and many big animals depend on them for food.
explain: «Antarctic krill are shrimp-like animals about 6 cm long, and all of them together may weigh hundreds of millions of tonnes.» One krill is small, but a huge crowd of them is very heavy.
explain: Krill sit in the middle of a food chain. They eat even tinier plankton, and they are eaten by whales, penguins, seals, fish and seabirds. If krill disappeared, many other animals would have less to eat.
fact: Krill are tiny shrimp-like sea animals that live in huge groups.
fact: Krill live in cold oceans, especially the Southern Ocean near Antarctica.
fact: Krill are food for whales, penguins, seals, fish and seabirds.
fact: A blue whale can eat tonnes of krill in one day.
fact: Whales with «baleen», rows of bristly plates in the mouth, sieve krill and small fish out of the water.
exercise: «Antarctic krill are shrimp-like animals about 6 cm long.» What are krill? | *Tiny shrimp-like sea animals | Large whales | Plants that float near the top of the sea | Birds that live on ice
exercise: Krill are food for many animals. Which animals eat krill? | Rocks and ice only | Trees growing on the land | Only other krill | *Whales, penguins and seals
exercise: «Whales have rows of bristly plates that sieve tiny krill out of the water.» What does sieve mean here? | Throw away | Freeze | Sing to | *Strain out, so only the small things are caught
test: Where do most Antarctic krill live? | In rivers in the middle of cities | At the top of tall mountains | In hot deserts far from water | *In the Southern Ocean near Antarctica
test: «A blue whale eats tonnes of krill a day.» What does tonnes mean? | Tiny pieces of plankton | *Very heavy weights, 1000 kg each | Small bags of food | Days of the week
exam: Why might more whales mean more krill? | Whales eat all the krill, so there are always fewer | *Whale poo feeds tiny floating plants, and those plants feed krill | Krill hide from whales under the ice | Krill grow bigger when whales come near
